{"author":"cursor[bot]","body":"### V2 transcript reassembly ignores agent-specific format

**Medium Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
The v2 `readTranscriptFromObjectTree` always uses `agent.ReassembleJSONL(chunks)` for chunk reassembly, while the v2 write path (`writeTranscriptBlobs`) uses agent-aware `agent.ChunkTranscript(ctx, redacted, opts.Agent)` for chunking. The equivalent v1 read function `readTranscriptFromTree` correctly uses `agent.ReassembleTranscript(chunks, agentType)`, which dispatches to agent-specific reassembly when the agent is known. This asymmetry means transcripts written by agents with custom (non-JSONL) chunking formats will be incorrectly reassembled when read back via the v2 path. The agent type is available in `ReadSessionContent` (from session metadata) but is never passed through to the transcript reading functions.
